ITEMS=[
("A bank directly engages an appraiser by contract for a lending assignment. Which USPAP role does the bank occupy because it engaged the appraiser?",
 ["Client","Other intended user","Party to the transaction","Appraisal reviewer"],
 "The client is the party that engages the appraiser, directly or through an agent. Being a lender or a party to the deal does not by itself make someone the client."),
("At assignment inception, the appraiser identifies a named credit union, in addition to the engaging bank, as a party expected to use the appraisal. Which role describes the credit union?",
 ["Other intended user","Client","Party receiving a copy only","Intended use"],
 "An intended user other than the client is identified by the appraiser based on communication with the client at assignment inception. Merely receiving a copy does not make a party an intended user."),
("The appraiser and client identify mortgage underwriting as the purpose for which the results will be used. Which assignment element is being established?",
 ["Intended use","Intended user","Scope of work","Type of value"],
 "Intended use identifies the use of the appraisal results, distinct from who will use them."),
("A report is signed in June but its value opinion applies to the property as of March 31. What does March 31 represent?",
 ["The effective date","The date of the report","The inspection date","The engagement date"],
 "The effective date is the date to which the analyses, opinions and conclusions apply, rather than the report signing date."),
("The condition of concealed structural members is uncertain as of the valuation date. With a reasonable basis and a credible result, an appraiser assumes they are sound; a contrary finding could change value. Which concept applies?",
 ["Extraordinary assumption","Hypothetical condition","Limiting condition","Jurisdictional exception"],
 "An extraordinary assumption concerns uncertain information that, if found false, could alter the conclusions. A hypothetical condition is contrary to what is known to exist."),
("For a permitted analytical purpose, an appraisal values a proposed house as already complete, although the appraiser knows construction has not begun at the effective date. Which concept applies?",
 ["Hypothetical condition","Extraordinary assumption","Prospective value opinion","Jurisdictional exception"],
 "A hypothetical condition is contrary to known facts as of the effective date; its use must satisfy USPAP requirements and be disclosed. A prospective opinion would use a future effective date."),
("A binding law prevents compliance with one particular USPAP requirement. The appraiser identifies and discloses the law and the affected requirement. Which rule addresses that conflict?",
 ["Jurisdictional Exception Rule","Competency Rule","Scope of Work Rule","Ethics Rule"],
 "The Jurisdictional Exception Rule applies to a conflict with applicable law or regulation, not a client preference."),
("An appraiser determines how much property identification, inspection, research and analysis is needed to produce credible results for an assignment. Which concept covers these decisions?",
 ["Scope of work","Competency","Problem identification","Assignment conditions"],
 "Scope of work is the type and extent of research and analyses in an assignment. Problem identification comes first and informs those decisions."),
("An appraiser develops a real property value opinion by identifying the problem and applying appropriate appraisal analyses. Which USPAP standard primarily governs this development work?",
 ["Standard 1","Standard 2","Standard 3","Standard 5"],
 "Standard 1 addresses developing a real property appraisal. Standard 2 covers reporting it, and Standard 5 concerns mass appraisal."),
("After developing a residential appraisal, an appraiser checks whether the written report communicates the results clearly and includes the required disclosures. Which standard primarily governs this reporting?",
 ["Standard 2","Standard 1","Standard 4","Standard 6"],
 "Standard 2 addresses reporting a real property appraisal. Standard 4 covers appraisal review reporting."),
("A reviewer researches whether another appraiser's work is credible and forms an opinion about its quality. Which standard primarily governs developing that appraisal review?",
 ["Standard 3","Standard 4","Standard 1","Standard 7"],
 "Standard 3 governs appraisal review development, including identifying the review problem and completing appropriate analyses."),
("A reviewer prepares the separate document communicating the review conclusions and supporting reasoning to the intended users. Which standard primarily governs that report?",
 ["Standard 4","Standard 3","Standard 2","Standard 8"],
 "Standard 4 governs appraisal review reporting; it requires clear, nonmisleading communication."),
("A fee agreement pays an appraiser only if a proposed loan closes, an event directly tied to the appraisal results. Which ethical problem is most directly present?",
 ["Contingent compensation","An undisclosed procurement payment","Improper advocacy","An interest in the property"],
 "USPAP prohibits compensation contingent on a subsequent event directly related to the appraiser's opinions and specific to the assignment's purpose."),
("An appraiser performed a property inspection for another purpose two years before accepting the current assignment but omits that fact from the required client disclosure and certification. Which problem is present?",
 ["Undisclosed prior service","Contingent compensation","Breach of confidentiality","Improper advocacy"],
 "Services regarding the subject in any capacity within the three years before accepting the assignment require disclosure, subject to confidentiality obligations."),
("An assistant inserts the appraiser's electronic signature on a new report under a general standing permission, without assignment-specific authorization. Which problem is present?",
 ["Unauthorized use of a signature","Failure to disclose significant assistance","Misleading electronic report transmission","Improper record keeping"],
 "Authorization to use an appraiser's signature must be specific to an assignment, not merely a blanket permission."),
("An appraiser selects assumptions specifically to promote the buyer's negotiating position rather than to produce an impartial value opinion. Which ethical problem is present?",
 ["Improper advocacy","Contingent compensation","Misleading extraordinary assumption","Undisclosed interest in the property"],
 "An appraiser must remain independent, impartial and objective and must not act as an advocate for a party's cause or interest in the appraisal."),
("A workfile is prepared January 10, 2026. The appraiser never testifies in a related judicial proceeding. Ignoring any longer requirement from another source, what date marks the end of the USPAP minimum retention period?",
 ["January 10, 2031","January 10, 2029","January 10, 2033","January 10, 2036"],
 "USPAP requires at least five years after preparation when the judicial-testimony extension does not apply: January 10, 2031."),
("A workfile is prepared January 10, 2026. The appraiser testifies in a related judicial proceeding that reaches final disposition January 10, 2030. What date ends the longer USPAP minimum period?",
 ["January 10, 2032","January 10, 2031","January 10, 2030","January 10, 2035"],
 "Compare five years after preparation (2031) with two years after final disposition (2032); the later date is January 10, 2032."),
("A workfile is prepared January 10, 2028. A judicial proceeding in which the appraiser provided testimony related to this assignment reaches final disposition January 10, 2029. What date ends the longer USPAP minimum period?",
 ["January 10, 2033","January 10, 2031","January 10, 2029","January 10, 2035"],
 "Five years after preparation ends in 2033; two years after final disposition ends in 2031. The later date, January 10, 2033, controls."),
("A workfile is prepared January 10, 2026. The appraiser provides testimony related to this assignment in a judicial proceeding with final disposition January 10, 2032. What date ends the longer USPAP minimum period?",
 ["January 10, 2034","January 10, 2031","January 10, 2032","January 10, 2037"],
 "The two-year judicial extension ends January 10, 2034, later than the five-year preparation period ending in 2031."),
("An engagement identifies a property and fee but leaves unclear who will rely on the opinion and for what purpose. Before deciding how much research is sufficient, which step addresses the missing problem definition?",
 ["Clarify the intended use and users","Expand the research and analysis","Adopt the lender's usual scope","Decline the assignment"],
 "Intended use and intended users are essential problem-identification elements that inform an acceptable scope of work."),
("During an otherwise workable assignment, new evidence reveals a second relevant market segment that the initial research did not address. Additional supported data can be obtained. Which response best addresses this scope issue?",
 ["Revise the scope and analyze the new data","Report the initial research as originally planned","Add an extraordinary assumption about the segment","Withdraw because the scope has changed"],
 "Scope decisions can change during an assignment. Obtain and analyze the additional evidence needed for credible results; an assumption is not a substitute for data that can be obtained."),
("A remaining uncertainty about a property characteristic has a reasonable basis, can be assumed without undermining credibility, and, if untrue, could change the conclusions. The extraordinary assumption is properly developed. What disclosure is required in the report?",
 ["State it and that it might have affected the results","Keep it in the workfile without mentioning it in the report","Convert it to a hypothetical condition","Obtain the client's written consent to the assumption"],
 "The extraordinary assumption and the fact that its use might have affected the assignment results must be clearly and conspicuously disclosed."),
("A client insists on a restriction that prevents credible results. Efforts to change it fail, and no permitted assumption or alternative analysis can solve the problem. What should the appraiser do?",
 ["Withdraw from the assignment","Complete it and disclose the restriction","Use a hypothetical condition to work around it","Complete it as a Restricted Appraisal Report"],
 "An appraiser cannot accept a scope limitation that makes the results noncredible; if it cannot be remedied, withdrawal is required. Disclosure or a different report option does not make the results credible."),
("Before agreeing to an unfamiliar property assignment, an appraiser determines that competence can be acquired in time. Which client communication must occur at this initial stage?",
 ["Disclose the lack of knowledge or experience before accepting","Disclose the gap only in the final report","Ask the client to waive the Competency Rule","Accept first, then notify the client if problems arise"],
 "The appraiser must disclose the lack of knowledge or experience before accepting, then acquire competence and describe the steps in the report."),
("An appraiser reasonably believed an assignment was familiar, but discovers a material competency gap midway through the work. What client communication is now required?",
 ["Notify the client of the gap","Mention the gap only in the certification","None, if the work is completed competently","Withdraw without contacting the client"],
 "If a lack of competence becomes apparent during an assignment, notify the client and comply with the remaining competency requirements."),
("After properly disclosing an initial knowledge gap, an appraiser obtains training and qualified assistance and completes the assignment competently. What must the final report say about that process?",
 ["Describe the lack of knowledge and the steps taken","Nothing, since the gap was disclosed at the start","Name the trainer and the qualified assistant","Certify the appraiser's experience with the property type"],
 "The report must describe the lack of knowledge or experience and the steps taken to complete the assignment competently. The earlier disclosure does not replace this."),
("An appraiser cannot obtain the specialized knowledge or assistance required to produce credible results within the assignment conditions. What is the appropriate competency decision?",
 ["Decline or withdraw from the assignment","Complete it and disclose the knowledge gap","Complete it under an extraordinary assumption","Use a Restricted Appraisal Report"],
 "If the appraiser cannot acquire the necessary competence, the assignment must be declined or ended rather than completed incompetently."),
("A neighboring owner asks for the confidential value conclusion in a completed assignment. No law, due process or other permitted disclosure applies. What is needed before giving that person the conclusion?",
 ["The client's authorization","A written request from the neighbor","The state regulator's approval","Redaction of the property address"],
 "A client may authorize disclosure to another party; a neighbor's request alone does not permit disclosure of assignment results."),
("The appraiser's state regulatory agency requests assignment records in its oversight role. Which response is consistent with USPAP confidentiality provisions, assuming no conflicting legal restriction?",
 ["Comply, since disclosure to the regulator is permitted","Refuse until the client authorizes release of the records","Provide only a redacted copy of the records","Refuse, since workfiles are always confidential"],
 "USPAP permits disclosure of confidential information or assignment results to state appraiser regulatory agencies without client authorization."),
("An appraiser wants to discuss broad trends publicly without client authorization. All confidential information and assignment results can be removed completely from the material. Which approach is permitted on those facts?",
 ["Use fully redacted, aggregated information","Use the results after removing only client names","Publish the results once a year has passed","Obtain each client's authorization first"],
 "Information that is fully aggregated or redacted so that no confidential information or assignment results remain can be disclosed without client authorization."),
("An appraiser leaves a firm that will retain the original workfiles. What action addresses the appraiser's continuing record-keeping obligation when personal custody is not maintained?",
 ["Arrange for access to and retrieval of the files","Make no arrangement since the firm keeps them","Destroy personal copies after leaving","Notify the state regulator of the move"],
 "The appraiser must have proper arrangements for retention, access and retrieval when someone else holds the workfiles."),
("An appraiser pays an outside intermediary to procure an assignment. Which fact belongs in the required procurement-fee disclosure, without requiring disclosure of the exact amount?",
 ["The fact of a referral payment","The exact dollar amount paid","The intermediary's business license number","The client's approval of the payment"],
 "The fact that a fee, commission or thing of value was paid to procure the assignment must be disclosed as required; the amount itself is not required."),
("An appraiser previously acted as the subject's selling agent 18 months before accepting an appraisal. Which relationship must be disclosed under the three-year service requirement?",
 ["Prior services concerning the property","An interest in the subject property","A broker referral fee arrangement","Significant appraisal assistance"],
 "Prior services in any capacity regarding the subject within the relevant three-year period include brokerage services."),
("An appraiser owns a small prospective purchase option in the subject property and is considering accepting an assignment. Which fact requires disclosure to the client and in the certification?",
 ["An interest in the subject property","Prior services regarding the subject property","The fee charged for the assignment","The option's purchase price"],
 "A current or prospective interest in the subject must be disclosed; impartiality remains required despite disclosure. The option's terms need not be stated."),
("A qualified colleague performs substantial valuation analysis but does not sign the certification. What contribution must the signing appraiser identify as required in the report and certification?",
 ["Significant appraisal assistance","Prior services regarding the property","The colleague's signature on the certification","The colleague's appraisal license number"],
 "Significant real property appraisal assistance must be addressed, including naming the person in the certification and describing the extent in the report."),
("A client requests anonymity in a written appraisal report. The report states that the identity is withheld at the client's request. What additional handling of that identity is required?",
 ["Keep a record of the client's identity in the workfile","State the client's identity in the certification","Give the identity to every intended user","No further handling is required"],
 "The client's identity must still be retained in the workfile even when the report uses the permitted anonymity statement."),
("A Restricted Appraisal Report will be used by the client and two additional parties. Which identification requirement specifically applies to those additional intended users?",
 ["Identify them by name","Identify them by type only","Name only the client","List them in the workfile only"],
 "Additional intended users of a Restricted Appraisal Report must be identified by name, not merely by a general type."),
("An appraiser determines that the income approach is not necessary for credible results in a particular assignment. What must the appraisal report explain about that omission?",
 ["Why the income approach was not developed","The income approach value it would have produced","That the results are less credible","Nothing, if the approach is unnecessary"],
 "The report must state the reasons for excluding an applicable valuation approach that was not developed."),
("An appraisal properly relies on an extraordinary assumption about an uncertain property characteristic. In addition to stating the assumption, what associated reporting disclosure is required?",
 ["That its use might have affected the results","That the assumption is guaranteed true","The probability that the assumption is false","The client's approval of the assumption"],
 "The report must state that use of the extraordinary assumption might have affected the assignment results; it does not require quantifying that effect."),
("In a market value assignment, the appraiser learns that the subject transferred twice during the three years before the effective date. The records are available. Which required analysis addresses this information?",
 ["Analyze the transfers and their circumstances","Report the transfers without analysis","Adjust value to the latest transfer price","Analyze only transfers in the past year"],
 "For market value, USPAP requires analysis of all sales and other transfers within the three years before the effective date when the information is available in the normal course of business. Listing them without analysis is not enough."),
("The applicable market value definition assumes the property was offered for sale for an adequate period before the hypothetical sale on the effective date. Which related opinion must be developed?",
 ["An opinion of reasonable exposure time","A marketing time forecast after the effective date","An opinion of the list price","An opinion of absorption period"],
 "When exposure time is a component of the definition, the appraiser develops a reasonable exposure-time opinion, which looks back before the effective date. Marketing time looks forward."),
("A proposed neighborhood adjustment uses a coded variable that appears to stand in for residents' race rather than a supported property characteristic. What issue must be investigated before using it?",
 ["Whether it is a proxy for a protected characteristic","Whether the variable is statistically significant","Whether the neighborhood boundary is drawn correctly","Whether the adjustment is bracketed by sales"],
 "USPAP prohibits using a proxy to conceal reliance on protected characteristics. Statistical significance does not make a biased adjustment acceptable."),
("An appraiser is ready to communicate an oral value conclusion but has not assembled any assignment workfile. Which record-keeping step must occur first?",
 ["Create the workfile before reporting","Obtain the client's approval of the oral report","Prepare a written report first","Record the conversation after it occurs"],
 "A workfile must be in existence before any report or other communication of assignment results, including an oral report."),
]
assert len(ITEMS)==44
